# What each level multiplies, read by .local/lib/machine-mode.sh (level_scale).
# The first row names the conf key each column scales; a key not named here is never scaled.
# A factor of 1 leaves the conf's value as it is, so mid is today's numbers. An integer stays an
# integer, and no factor takes a nonzero limit to 0, so no level turns a gate off.
#   DISPATCH_PER_PASS, DISPATCH_MAX_LOAD   fleet-dispatch's start limits
#   CLAUDE_ACCT_PACE_SLACK_PCT, CLAUDE_ACCT_RESERVE_PCT         claude-acct room, automatic starts only:
#     column keys for pace.conf's PACE_SLACK_PCT and RESERVE_PCT; no env var of that name is read
# Reserve falls as the level rises: high keeps less of each account back.
# high scales DISPATCH_MAX_LOAD by only 1.1: at the conf's 0.9 that is 0.99 a core, under home-config's
# NodeLoadHigh line (load15 over 1.0x cores), and full, the 01:00-06:00 mode, runs at high (ask mUmPN3, a).

level|DISPATCH_PER_PASS|DISPATCH_MAX_LOAD|CLAUDE_ACCT_PACE_SLACK_PCT|CLAUDE_ACCT_RESERVE_PCT
low|0.34|0.6|0.2|1.33
mid|1|1|1|1
high|2|1.1|2|0.67
